# Console TTY restrictions — deployed by Ansible
# Only listed TTYs allow root login. pam_securetty.so enforces this.
# LOGIN-4: no pseudo-terminal entry is listed here — that is what keeps a
# network-terminated session (SSH included) from ever presenting a tty
# this file accepts for direct root login.

# Virtual console TTYs (KVM/physical console)
tty1
tty2
tty3
tty4
tty5
tty6

# Serial console TTYs (some hosters use serial instead of VT)
ttyS0
ttyS1
